WEBVTT

NOTE Tacet film — generated by design/film/render.mjs from the voiceover file

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.100
How does an apprentice know what to ask?

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:09.700
Tacet reads the page directly, redacted before anything
leaves. Screen frames are the second path.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.200
Mira guesses before the expert decides. The gap is the
signal.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.200
Hypotheses compete. Information gained versus
interruption cost picks one question, at a pause.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.300
Voice is ElevenLabs, but the brain is Tacet's own
endpoint: it decides what is said, and when.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:35.700
Answers are compiled, not summarized: a rule, a
narrowing threshold, replayed on past cases.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:44.134
Proof: fresh cases, hashed before labels. Eleven of
eleven. Then an agent takes the same test over MCP and

00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:46.600
earns permission, rule by rule.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.280
The tutor stops a wrong save in the expert's words, in
any language. Same engine, new tasks.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.790
What you say becomes a rule. What you do proves it.
